\par \tab When this spell is cast, the wizard teleports desired items directly to his hand. The objects must be naturally occurring components for spells the wizard knows and they must be within spell range. The c
omponents must be items commonly found in the area, such as a twig, feather, firefly, or bit of beeswax in a forest.
\par \tab If the components lie underground or underwater at a depth greater than 10 feet, they cannot be conjured, even if the caster is at a similar depth (such as in a cavern or at the bottom of a lake).
