\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 1d4 rounds +1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 1
\par Area of Effect: One creature/level
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell increases the amount of time a character can hold his breath. As described in the }{\i\fs24 Player's Handbook}{\fs24 , a character can hold his breath for a num
ber of rounds equal to one-third his Constitution score. The effect of this spell is added to that figure.
\par \tab The duration of the spell is always unknown to the recipient; the DM secretly rolls 1d4 to determine the exact duration. At the end of this time, the character must succeed a Constitution check or be forced to take a breath as per the rules. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Metamorphose Liquids}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Permanent
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: 1'-cube/level
\par Saving Throw: Special
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell transmutes one type of liquid into an equal amount of a different, nonmagical fluid (water, wine, blood, oil, apple cider, etc.). The caster must touch the fluid itself (not simply its container) for the spell to take effect.
\par \tab Magical liquid
s (such as potions) receive a saving throw vs. disintegration with a +3 bonus to avoid the spell's effect. Fluids can be transmuted only into nonmagical liquids; it is not possible to change a magical liquid into another type of magical liquid. Poisons ma
y be rendered harmless through use of this spell, but the spell has no effect on poisons already consumed.
\par \tab Living creatures are unaffected by the spell, excluding those from the elemental plane of water. Such creatures are allowed a saving throw vs. spell.
 Failure results in 1d4 points of damage per level of the caster, while success indicates half damage. Only one creature can be affected by a single casting of this spell, regardless of the creature's size.
\par \tab The material component is a drop of the liquid that the caster intends to create, which must be placed on the wizard's tongue and consumed. Creating poisons through use of this spell is especially dangerous. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Murdock's Feathery Flyer}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 1
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None Upon casting this spell, a feathery membrane grows under the 
\par wizard's arms, extending along his sides all the way to his feet. The membrane appears to 
\par merge with the caster's skin and clothing. 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab 
If the caster spreads his arms and jumps from a height, he may glide through the air. For each foot of elevation, the wizard can glide five feet horizontally. Thus, a wizard jumping from a 10-foot wall could glide up to 50 feet. Gliding characters have 
a movement rate of 12 and Maneuverability Class E. A wizard attempting to carry more than his normal weight allowance plummets to the earth upon takeoff.
\par \tab When the spell expires, the feathers instantly disappear. If the wizard is airborne, he immediately plummets toward the ground.
\par \tab The material component is an eagle's feather.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Nahal's Reckless Dweomer*}{\b\fs24  (Invocation/Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Special
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: Special
