\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab By touching the remains of a dead creature, this spell allows a caster to gain a mental image of the deceased's former appearance. The remains can be of any age and only a tiny fragment is required, such as a bone splinter or a strand of hair.
\par \tab When cast by a wizard of at least 7th level, he is able to view the final minute of the subject's life from the subject's point of view.
\par \tab When cast by a wizard of at least 9th level, a personal possession (a ring, a favorite walking stick, etc.) may be substituted for bodily remains.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Protection From Paralysis}{\b\fs24  (Abjuration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn/level
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab The recipient of this spell receives total immunity to magical paralysis. Spells such as }{\i\fs24 hold person}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 slow}{\fs24 
 have no effect on the individual. This spell also provides protection against the paralysis attacks of monsters (a ghoul's touch, for example). This spell offers no protection against physical damage.
\par \tab The material component is a bit of cloth taken from a priest's robes. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Ride the Wind}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 5 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn/level
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: One creature/level
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows creatures targeted by the caster to become virtually weightless and be lifted upon the wind. Affected creatures can control their altitude by rising or descending at a
 movement rate of 12, but are at the mercy of the wind for speed and direction. Recipients can stop forward movement only by grasping something to anchor them in place. If no wind is present, this spell has no effect.
\par \tab Unwilling targets are allowed a saving throw to resist the effect.
\par \tab Each subject and his equipment must weigh less than 100 pounds per level of the caster. Thus, a 6th-level wizard could affect six creatures each weighing 600lbs. or less. This spell may be cast only on living creatures.
\par \tab The material components are a small handful of straw and a dry leaf. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Sense Shifting}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 3 turns
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\i\fs24 
\par \tab Sense shifting}{\fs24  allows the wizard to affect all sp
ells of levels 1 through 3 that he casts within the duration of the spell. For each spell, he can modify one of three sensory features pertaining to the spell: color, sound, or patterned visual appearance of the spell effect. The changes produced by this 
spell do not affect the functions of the affected spell nor any saving throws that apply against their effects.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Sense shifting}{\fs24  might be used to produce green }{\i\fs24 fireballs, magic missiles}{\fs24  that streak through the air with a scream, colored}{\i\fs24  continual light}{\fs24  globes, customized designs for a }{\i\fs24 
hypnotic pattern}{\fs24 , or a }{\i\fs24 spectral hand}{\fs24  that makes scrabbling sounds as it attempts to grasp a target.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Sense shifting}{\fs24  cannot create any form of invisibility. It cannot completely silence a spell effect (thus, a }{\i\fs24 fireball's}{\fs24  blast might be muted, but not wholly eliminated).
\par \tab The material component is a twist of multi-colored ribbon with a small silver bell fastened to its end. 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs36\cf2 
\par Third-Level Spells }{\fs24 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Alacrity}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn+1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 1
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab The use of an }{\i\fs24 alacrity}{\fs24  spell allows the wizard to speed up the casting of spells of 5th level and lower. Only spells that are cast within the }{\i\fs24 alacrity}{\fs24  spell's duration are affected.
\par \tab Casting times of 2-5 are reduced by 1; casting times of 6-9 are reduced by 2; and a casting time of one round is reduced to a casting time of 8. Casting times for spells which require more than 1 round are reduced by 20% (e.g., an }{\i\fs24 
animate dead}{\fs24  spell affected by }{\i\fs24 alacrity}{\fs24  could be cast in only 4 rounds). Spells which have a casting time of 1 are not affected by this spell.
\par \tab The material component is a miniature hourglass which is destroyed when the spell is cast. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Alamir's Fundamental Breakdown}{\b\fs24  (Divination) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: One item
\par Saving Throw: Special
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab By casting this spell, the wizard learns what ingredients and formulas were used to create a chemical mixture or magical item.
\par \tab The information 
instantly appears in the caster's mind but may be lost if the wizard cannot comprehend it. The caster must roll an Intelligence check; if successful, the wizard understands the formula and retains it in his memory. If the roll is missed, the caster cannot
 comprehend what he has learned and the information is immediately forgotten. If the spell is cast a second time on the same substance, the spell automatically fails unless the wizard has advanced to the next experience level.
\par \tab The caster's level determines the type of information gleaned:
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 5th Level:}{\fs24  The type and quantity of ingredients and the preparation process required to produce a non-magical mixture are learned. For example, the wizard could learn how to produce Greek fire or gunpowder, or could learn
 the recipe for something simple, like chocolate cake.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 9th Level: }{\fs24 The wizard may learn the proper ingredients and formula for making a magical liquid (potion, scroll ink, etc.).
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 14th Level: }{\fs24 The caster may learn the formula for creating any type of magical object, excluding unique items and objects of extreme power (artifacts and relics).
\par \tab In all cases, simply knowing the proper formula does not mean the wizard can successfully create the item or material. The construction of alchemical mixtures and magical items is a time-consuming and expensive undertaking.
\par \tab This spell has detrimental effects on the magical item analyzed. Single-use items (potions, oils, etc.) are automatically destroyed; the spell consumes the item in the process of analyzing it. Reusabl
e magical items must make a saving throw vs. disintegration. If the saving throw is failed,}{\i\fs24  Alamir's fundamental breakdown}{\fs24 
 releases the magic of the item in an explosive blast, rendering it permanently nonmagical. The caster suffers 4d8 points of damage from the explosion.
\par \tab The material component is a wand cut from a 100-year-old oak tree. The wand is used to touch the item in question, and vanishes in a puff of smoke when the spell is complete. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Alternate Reality*}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Instantaneous
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: Creature touched
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab With this spell, the caster creates a small variation in probabilities. This variation lasts only a moment, but creates alternate results for one recent event. 
When the spell is cast, any one event attempted by the recipient during the previous round is recalculated, essentially allowing (or forcing) the creature to make new die rolls.
\par \tab Only events that begin and end in a single round can be affected. Only one di
e roll can be rerolled. If the creature touched is a willing recipient, the player can choose which roll (the original or the new roll) affects him, more than likely picking the most successful. If the creature is unwilling, he must redo the action. The s
econd result, whatever its outcome, cannot be changed.
\par \tab Typical uses of this spell include allowing a fighter to reroll an attack, forcing an opponent to reroll a saving throw, or allowing a wizard to reroll the damage caused by a fireball.
\par The material component is a small, unmarked die. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Augmentation I}{\b\fs24  (Invocation/Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell augments the damage inflicted by any spell of levels 1-3. For each die of damage rolled, the caster adds one point to the damage total.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 augmentation I}{\fs24  spell affects only one spell cast on the round immediately following the }{\i\fs24 augmentation}{\fs24 . If an entire round or more elapses, the }{\i\fs24 augmentation}{\fs24  is wasted.
\par \tab Only spells which cause direct physical damage are affected by }{\i\fs24 augmentation}{\fs24 ; for example, monsters gained through }{\i\fs24 monster summoning I}{\fs24  gain no bonuses to their damage.
\par \tab The material component is a pair of concentric circles of bronze or silver. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Far Reaching I}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Component: V
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows the wizard to extend the range of any one 1st- or 2nd-level spell by 50% or any one 3rd-level spell by 25%. The spell to be affected must be cast on the round immediately following the }{\i\fs24 far reaching I}{\fs24 
 spell. If a complete round or more elapses, the }{\i\fs24 far reaching I}{\fs24  is wasted.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Far reaching I}{\fs24  affects only a spell cast by the same wizard. }{\i\fs24 Far reaching I}{\fs24  does not affect spells that have range of 0 or touch. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Fireflow*}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: One fire source
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows a wizard to control natural fires by manipulating randomness an
d adjusting probabilities to cause them to spread and take shape in any direction he desires. Once cast, the wizard points at any fire within range. He can then cause that fire to move in any direction desired within spell range, as long as the flames con
tact a solid surface (the fire may not be raised in the air).
\par \tab The caster must maintain concentration or the spell fails. The flames can be spread at the rate of 50 square feet per turn. Thus, if a caster affects a campfire, he could create a flaming line 1
 foot wide and 50 feet long or fill a 5' 0 10' square in a single round.
\par \tab The flames are not limited by a lack of burnable material and can be directed to spread over water, snow, ice, and other nonflammable surfaces. The surface is not harmed, but objects
 and creatures caught in the flames suffer damage as if they had stepped into the original fire source. Thus, a character caught in flames created from a candle will suffer only minor damage, while a character caught in a blaze that originated from a huge
 bonfire will be severely burned.
\par \tab The material components are a small paintbrush and a pot of pitch. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Fool's Speech*}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 hour/level
\par Casting Time: 1 turn
\par Area of Effect: Caster+1 creature/level
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab With this spell, the wizard empowers himself and others of his choosing with the ability to speak a secret language incomprehensible to others. Creatures designated to speak the language must be touching each other when the spell is cast.
\par \tab Once cast, the characters can choose to speak normally or in their secret tongue. They can speak and understand this mysterious language fluently.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Fool's speech}{\fs24  is not recognizable as any known language, nor does it remotely sound like any language. A }{\i\fs24 comprehend languages}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 tongues}{\fs24 
 spell will not translate it. It can be understood by a character wearing a }{\i\fs24 helm of comprehending languages and reading magic}{\fs24 , although the normal percentage chances apply.
\par \tab The material component is a small whistle made of bone.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Lorloveim's Creeping Shadow}{\b\fs24  (Illusion) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 7
\par Area of Effect: The caster's shadow
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 \tab 
\par \tab This spell causes the wizard's shadow to elongate, stretching away from his body at a rate of 15 yards per round. It can elongate a maximum distance of 10 yards per level of the caster.
\par \tab The shadow moves as an ordinary shadow, along floors and up walls. The caster may maneuver in any manner feasible to place the shadow where he desires. A cas
ter might position his shadow over a high window in a tower in order to spy on the tower's occupants. The shadow makes no sound and is 90% undetectable in all but the brightest surroundings.
\par \tab While the spell lasts, the illusionist can see, hear, and speak 
through his shadow. The shadow cannot physically touch, pick up, or attack creatures or objects. It can be struck only by spells, magical weapons of +1 or better, or other special attacks (such as a dragon's breath). The shadow has the same Armor Class as
 the caster. Hit points lost by the shadow are suffered by the caster.
\par \tab To cast the spell, a light source of at least the brightness of a candle must be present.
\par \tab The material component is a small statuette of the caster sculpted from a piece of obsidian worth at least 1,000 gp. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Maximilian's Stony Grasp}{\b\fs24  (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 20 yards+10 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 5 rounds+1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Special
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell must be cast on stony ground,
 such as a manmade stone floor, a natural cavern floor, or a boulder-strewn field. It is not possible to cast the spell on a stone wall or ceiling. The spell causes an arm made of stone (about the same size as a normal human limb) to rise from the ground 
b
eneath any creature targeted by the caster. The stony hand attempts to grasp the leg of the targeted creature, who is allowed a saving throw to avoid the effect; if the save is successful, the hand disappears. Each round thereafter, the hand has a 5% chan
ce per level of the caster of reappearing and attacking.
\par \tab Creatures grasped by the hand suffer a movement rate of 0, AC penalty of -2, and attack penalty of -2. Grasped characters lose any Dexterity bonuses. The hand causes no damage to its victim.
\par \tab The stony limb has AC 2 and hit points equal to triple the caster's maximum hit points. The maximum number of hit points a stony hand may have is 60.
\par \tab The material component is a miniature hand sculpted from stone, which crumbles to dust when the conjured hand is destroyed or the spell expires. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Minor Malison}{\b\fs24  (Enchantment/Charm) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 60 feet
\par Component: V
\par Duration: 2 rounds/level
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: 30-foot-radius sphere
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows a wizard to adversely affect all the saving throws of his enemies. Opponents under the influence of this spell make all saving throws at a penalty of -1.
\par \tab Alternatively, the wizard may select any one school of magic and cause his enemies to make all saving throws against magic from that school a
t -2. This penalty is not cumulative with a saving throw penalty derived from the wizard being a specialist; the penalty is not increased to -3. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Spirit Armor}{\b\fs24  (Necromancy) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 2 rounds/level
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: Special
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 \tab 
\par \tab This spell allows the wizard to surround himself with a portion of his own life essence, which takes the form of a shimmering aura. The }{\i\fs24 spirit armor}{\fs24  offers protection equivalent to splint mail (AC 4) and grants the wiza
rd a +3 bonus to saving throws vs. magical attacks. The }{\i\fs24 spirit armor's}{\fs24  effects are not cumulative with other types of armor or magical protection, but Dexterity bonuses apply.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 spirit armor}{\fs24  is effective against magical and nonmagical weapons and attacks. It does not hinder movement or add weight or encumbrance. It does not interfere with spellcasting.
\par \tab When the spell ends, the aura dissipates and the caster temporarily loses a bit of his life essence, suffering 2d3 points of damage unless he succeeds at
 a saving throw vs. spell. No damage is sustained if the save is successful. The hit points lost can be regained only through magical healing. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Squaring the Circle}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\i\fs24 
\par \tab Squaring the circle}{\fs24  allows a wizard to alter the shape of the area of effect of one spell of 1st- through 5th-level spells. The spell to be affected must be cast within the duration of the }{\i\fs24 squaring the circle spell}{\fs24 .
\par \tab S
quare or cubic areas of effect can be transformed into circular or spherical areas of effect. Circular or spherical areas of effect can likewise be transformed into square or cubic areas of effect. In both cases, the length of a side of a square area is e
quated to the diameter of a circular or spherical area.
\par \tab Alternatively, a square or cubic area can be transformed into a rectangle. The rectangle cannot cover more or less square footage than the standard square area of the spell.
\par \tab Similarly, a circular or spherical area can be transformed into an oval or egg shape. The area covered by the oval or egg shape cannot cover more or less square footage than the original area of the spell.
\par \tab The material component is a small pendant of any precious metal with a circle fashioned inside a square. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Watery Double}{\b\fs24  (Conjuration/Summoning, Enchantment) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: Special; max. 10 rounds
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: One body of liquid
\par Saving Throw: Neg. 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell may be cast on any body
 of liquid as large as an ocean or as small as a glass of wine. The first creature whose reflection is cast on the surface of the liquid releases the spell. When the spell is triggered, the liquid immediately forms an exact three-dimensional image of the 
reflected creature. If more than one creature casts a reflection simultaneously, only one watery double forms. Each creature has an equal chance of being the victim of the spell (roll randomly).
\par \tab The size of the }{\i\fs24 watery double}{\fs24  is restricted by the volume of fluid available. If the spell were cast on a full mug of ale, the double would form from the ale, becoming a mug-sized duplicate of the victim. The}{\i\fs24  watery double
}{\fs24  will never exceed the actual size of the victim regardless of the size of the body of liquid.
\par \tab When the spell is cast on the liquid, its duration is considered permanent until the power is released by a creature's reflection. The liquid will not evaporate until the spell is triggered. When the}{\i\fs24  watery double}{\fs24 
 forms, it remains animated for 1 round per experience level of the caster, to a maximum of 10 rounds.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 watery double}{\fs24  attempts to touch the creature it has duplicated. It can affect only the creature that it resembles. It has the same THAC0 and current hit points as the creature it duplicates,
 but cannot cast spells or use any of the creature's magical items or special abilities. The }{\i\fs24 watery double}{\fs24  is AC 6 and its movement rate is double that of the victim. It may seep under doors and through cracks.
\par \tab If the }{\i\fs24 watery double}{\fs24  succeeds in touching th
e creature, it merges with the individual, covering his entire body in a skin of liquid. The victim must attempt a saving throw. If successful, the creature has resisted the spell's effect and the }{\i\fs24 watery double}{\fs24 
 "dies," becoming normal fluid (and soaking the creature in the process). If the saving throw is failed, the}{\i\fs24  watery double}{\fs24  begins forcing its way into the victim's body, inflicting 1d8 points of damage per round until it is destroyed.

\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 watery double}{\fs24  dissipates if reduced to zero hit points or when the spell's duration expires. Striking the watery double while it is wrapped around its victim causes an equal amount of damage to the victim. }{\i\fs24 
Part water, lower water}{\fs24 , and }{\i\fs24 transmute water to dust}{\fs24  spells instantly destroy a }{\i\fs24 watery double}{\fs24 . 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Wizard Sight}{\b\fs24  (Divination) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Upon completion of this spell, the caster's eyes glow blue and he is able to see the magical auras of spellcasters and enchanted o
bjects. Only the auras of those things normally visible to the caster are seen; this spell does not grant the wizard the ability to see invisible objects, nor does it give him X-ray vision. This spell does not reveal the presence of good or evil or reveal
 alignment.
\par \tab While }{\i\fs24 wizard sight}{\fs24 
 is in effect, a wizard is able to see whether someone is a spellcaster and whether that person is a priest or a wizard (and what type of specialist, if any). He can sense if a nonspellcaster has the potential to learn and cas
t wizard spells (e.g., whether a fighter will someday gain the ability to cast a spell).
\par \tab Although a spellcaster's level cannot be discerned, the wizard can see the intensity of a spellcaster's aura and guess at the individual's magical power (dim, faint, 
moderate, strong, overwhelming). This can be extremely ambiguous even when a wizard has some method of comparison; the DM might announce that a subject's intensity is roughly equivalent to that of a companion, or he might announce that a subject's aura is
 the strongest the wizard has ever encountered.
\par \tab An object's magical abilities cannot be discerned. The fact that it is magical and the type of magic (abjuration, alteration, etc.) are obvious. The wizard can see the intensity of an item's magical aura and 
guess at its power, but cannot tell whether a magical item is cursed. 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs36\cf2 Fourth-Level Spells }{\fs24 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Dilation I}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Component: V
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\i\fs24 
\par \tab Dilation I}{\fs24  allows a wizard to increase the area of effect of any one spell of levels 1-3. The area of effect is increased by 25%; thus, a }{\i\fs24 stinking cloud}{\fs24 
 would fill a 25-foot cube, while a slow spell would affect creatures in a 50-foot cube. Fractions of feet or yards (as appropriate to the spell) are dropped.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Dilation I}{\fs24 
 must be cast immediately prior to the spell to be dilated; if a complete round or more elapses, the dilation is wasted. The dilation spell affects only spells which have areas of effect defined in feet or yards (numbers of cr
eatures cannot be increased). The dilation affects only spells cast by the same wizard. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Divination Enhancement}{\b\fs24  (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Component: V
\par Duration: 2 turns+2 rounds/level
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows a wizard to extend both the duration and range of the }{\i\fs24 wizard eye}{\fs24  spell and any divination spells of levels 1-4. Duration and range are both increased by 50% for the length of the }{\i\fs24 divination enhancement}{
\fs24 .
\par \tab All divination spells cast within the duration of the enhancement are increased. The expiration of the enhancement cancels all divination spells in effect. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Far Reaching II}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Component: V
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell's function is identical to the 3rd-level }{\i\fs24 far reaching I}{\fs24 
 spell, except that a spell of 1st or 2nd level has its range doubled and a spell of 3rd level has its range increased by 50%. In addition, any spell of 4th level has its range extended by 25%. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Greater Malison}{\b\fs24  (Enchantment/Charm) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 60 feet
\par Component: V
\par Duration: 2 rounds/level
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: 30-foot-radius sphere
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell operates exactly like the 3rd-level }{\i\fs24 minor malison}{\fs24  spell except that the wizard places 
a -2 penalty on all saving throws of all hostile creatures within the area of effect. Optionally, the wizard may create a -3 penalty to saving throws against spells from one school of magic. This penalty is not cumulative with a saving throw penalty which
 derived from the wizard being a specialist; the penalty is not increased to -4. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Locate Creature}{\fs24  }{\b\fs24 (Divination)}{\fs24  
\par Range: 50 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn/level
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell is similar to the 2nd-level }{\i\fs24 locate object}{\fs24 
 spell. Instead of finding an inanimate object, however, it allows the wizard to find a creature. The wizard casts the spell, slowly turns, and is able to sense the direction of the person or creature, provided the su
bject is within range. The wizard learns how far away the creature is and in what direction it is moving (if at all).
\par \tab This spell can locate a general species of creature (a horse or umber hulk, for instance) or can be used to find a specific individual. T
he wizard must have physically seen the individual or the type of creature at least once from a distance of no more than 10 yards.
\par \tab Unlike }{\i\fs24 locate object}{\fs24 , this spell is not blocked by lead. It is blocked, however, by running water (such as a river or stream). Objects cannot be found through use of this spell.
\par \tab The material component is a bit of a bloodhound's fur.  
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Mask of Death}{\b\fs24  (Necromancy) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 hour/level
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab By casting this spell, a wizard can change a corpse's features to make it appear to be someone else. The caster must possess an accurate portrait of the individual to be duplicated, or must have a clear mental image of the person based on pers
onal experience.
\par \tab If }{\i\fs24 animate dead}{\fs24  is cast on the body, it can be animated to become a zombie that looks exactly like the copied person. The double is a mindless automaton, however, having all the characteristics of a normal zombie.
\par \tab This spell may be cast on a creature that has already become a zombie. The wizard must successfully touch the zombie in combat, unless the zombie is controlled by the caster.
\par \tab The material component of this spell is a drop of doppleganger's blood. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Minor Spell Turning}{\b\fs24  (Abjuration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 3 rounds/level
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell is similar to the 7th-level }{\i\fs24 spell turning}{\fs24 , which causes spells cast against the wizard to rebound on the original caster. 
This includes spells cast from scrolls and innate spell-like abilities, but excludes the following: area effects that are not centered directly upon the protected wizard, spell effects delivered by touch, and spell effects from devices such as wands, stav
es, and so forth. Thus, a }{\i\fs24 light}{\fs24 
 spell cast to blind the protected wizard could be turned back upon and possibly blind the caster, while the same spell would be unaffected if cast to light an area in which the protected wizard were standing.
\par \tab One to four (1d4) spell levels may be turned. The exact number is secretly rolled by the DM; the player never knows how effective the spell is.
\par \tab Unlike the 7th level version of this spell, }{\i\fs24 minor spell turning}{\fs24  is not capable of partially turning a spell. For example, if a
 wizard has three levels of spell turning, he can turn three 1st-level spells, one 1st and one 2nd, or one 3rd-level spell. He can in no way turn spells of 4th level or above. If the caster is the target of a spell of a higher level than he is capable of 
turning, the caster receives the full brunt of the spell.
\par \tab If the protected wizard and a spellcasting attacker both have spell turning effects operating, a resonating field is created that has the following effects:
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx900\adjustright {\b\fs24 D100 
\par Roll \tab Effect }{\fs24 
\par 01-70 \tab Spell drains away without effect 
\par 71-80 \tab Spell affects both equally at full damage 
\par 81-97 \tab Both turning effects are rendered non-functional for 1d4 turns 
\par 98-00 \tab Both casters are sucked through a rift into the Positive Material plane 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab The material component of this spell is a smoothly polished silver coin. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Mordenkainen's Celerity}{\b\fs24  (Alteration, Invocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par }\pard\plain \s1\keep\keepn\nowidctlpar\tx360\outlinelevel0\adjustright {Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard\plain \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright \fs20 {\i\fs24 
\par \tab Mordenkainen's celerity}{\fs24  affects spells of levels 1-3 which alter the movement of the wizard such as }{\i\fs24 feather fall, jump, spider climb, levitate, fly}{\fs24 , and }{\i\fs24 haste}{\fs24 
. Spells to be affected must be cast within 1 turn of the casting of the celerity. Spells do not expire when the celerity expires.
\par \tab Spells cast following the celerity receive a 25% bonus to duration. This effect may not be gained in conjunction with other means of magically extending a spell's duration. In addition, the caster's movement rate is increased by 25%. }{\i\fs24 
Feather fall}{\fs24  is an exception; the rate of descent may be reduced by 25% at the caster's option.
\par \tab The area of effect is always the caster, except in the case of the }{\i\fs24 haste}{\fs24  spell, for which the effects of the celerity will operate on 1d4 creatures in addition to the wizard. The celerity will not affect
 the other creatures in any other manner.
\par \tab The celerity gives the wizard a +2 bonus to his saving throws against spells of levels 1-3 which directly affect his movement. This includes }{\i\fs24 web, hold person}{\fs24 , and }{\i\fs24 slow}{\fs24 . The wizard also gains a +2 bonus on all savi
ng throws against magical paralysis attacks.
\par \tab The material component is a small pouch or vessel containing centipede or millipede legs. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Summon Lycanthrope}{\b\fs24  (Conjuration/Summoning) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Special
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 1 turn
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell is effective only on the night of a full moon and one night immediately preceding and following it.
\par \tab For the spell to be effective, the caster and the lycanthrope must be on the same plane of exi
stence; there is no other range limitation. When the spell is cast, the nearest lycanthrope (as determined by the DM) of the chosen species must attempt a saving throw. If successful, the creature is unaffected. If it fails, the lycanthrope instantly appe
ars near the caster.
\par \tab Upon arrival, the creature can freely attack the wizard unless the caster has created a warding circle. If a circle is present, the lycanthrope appears in the circle; otherwise, it appears 1d10 feet away from the caster in a random dir
ection (the DM should use the scatter diagram for grenade-like missiles found in the }{\i\fs24 DUNGEON MASTER}{\fs24 \'ae Guide to determine direction).
\par \tab A warding circle is a temporary prison drawn with specially prepared pigments laced with silver filings. These pigments cos
t 100 gp for each foot of diameter of the circle (thus, a circle 10 feet across costs 1,000 gp). A warding circle must be at least 5 feet in diameter; if smaller, the lycanthrope is automatically freed. Preparing the circle takes one turn per foot of diam
eter.
\par \tab Even with such protection, the lycanthrope can break out of the circle and wreak vengeance upon the summoner. The creature's base chance of success is 20%, modified by the difference between its Hit Dice and the wizard's experience level. If the spel
lcaster is of a higher level, the difference is subtracted from the creature's chance of escaping the circle. If the lycanthrope is of higher Hit Dice than the wizard's level, the difference is added to its chance. Each creature is allowed only one attemp
t to escape.
\par \tab Any break in the circle spoils the power of the spell and enables the lycanthrope to break free. Even a straw dropped across the line of a magic circle destroys its power. Fortunately, the creature cannot take any action against any portion of
 the ward, for the magic of the barrier absolutely prevents this.
\par \tab Once safely ensnared, the lycanthrope can be held for as long as the summoner dares. The creature cannot leave the circle, nor can any of its attacks or powers penetrate the magical barrier
. When the full moon sets, the lycanthrope reverts to its human form. At this time, it is free of the spell and may leave the circle.
\par \tab The material components are a drop of blood from any animal, a human hair, and a moonstone worth at least 150 gp. If the caster elects to create the warding circle, the components described above are also required. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 There/Not There*}{\b\fs24  (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1-6 turns
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: 10' cube
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This peculiar wild magic creates a random fluctuation in the probabilities of existence. The spell can be cast only upon nonliving objects and can affect only materials within a 10'x10'x10' cube.
\par \tab Objects in the area of effect either remain normal and visible or
 they disappear (50% chance). The state of existence for any object is determined randomly and changes with each viewing and viewer. Thus, a single object could appear and disappear several times during the course of the spell. Furthermore, it might be "t
here" for one onlooker, but "not there" for another.
\par \tab For example, a wild mage casts this spell on a doorway. The DM rolls percentile dice and determines the door is "there" for the wizard. The wizard's companion also looks at the door. The DM rolls and det
ermines that the door is "not there" for the companion. The pair studies the door for several minutes, during which time the door does not change (this counts as a single viewing for each character).
\par \tab The wizard and his companion then close their eyes. Whe
n they look at the door again, new checks for each character reveal the door is "not there" for both characters. The pair steps through the open archway and turns around to look at the door once again. This time it is "not there" for the wizard, but "ther
e" for his companion. This random changing continues throughout the duration of the spell.
\par \tab Objects that are "there" are normal in all respects. Doors can be opened, chests can be picked up and carried, and rocks can be used as barricades. Objects that are 
"not there" are gone, although their absence does not cause ceilings to collapse or other damage. A wizard could walk through a "not there" wall without difficulty.
\par \tab When two parties perceive a }{\i\fs24 there/not there}{\fs24  object differently, the object functions for e
ach party according to its own perceptions. For example, a wizard hides behind a rock that he sees as "there." Her enemy, a fighter, perceives the rock as "not there" and fires arrows at the wizard. The wizard would perceive the arrows as bouncing off the
 
rock, while the fighter would perceive the arrows as missing their target or falling short. The fighter would be subject to a check before firing each arrow to determine whether his perception changes (assume that the fighter must look away from the rock 
every time he nocks an arrow; each time he takes aim, this counts as a new viewing).
\par \tab After the spell is cast, any objects removed from the area of effect retain their uncertain existence for the duration of the spell. Thus, a pair of heroes could pick up a
 treasure chest, carry it down the hall, set it down, and discover it had vanished while their backs were turned. Worse still, one might see the chest and the other not!
\par The material component is a small piece of cat fur sealed inside a small box. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Thunder Staff }{\b\fs24 (Invocation/Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Instantaneous
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: 20'x40' cone
\par Saving Throw: 1/2 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Upon completion of this spell, the wizard raps his staff on the ground and produces a thundering cone of 
force 5' wide at the apex, 20' wide at the base, and 40' long. All creatures wholly or partially within this cone must roll a successful saving throw or be stunned for 1d3 rounds. Stunned creatures are unable to think coherently or act during this time an
d
 are deafened for 1d3+1 rounds. Additionally, those who fail the save are hurled 4d4+4 feet by the wave of force, suffering 1 point of damage per two feet thrown. Intervening surfaces (walls, doors, etc.) may restrict this distance, but damage remains the
 same (4d4+4). 
\par \tab If the save is successful, the victim is not stunned, but is deafened for 1d3+1 rounds and is hurled only half the distance.
\par \tab Giant-sized or larger creatures who succeed at their saving throws are deafened but are not thrown, suffer no loss
 of hit points, and are not stunned. If the saving throw is failed, such creatures are hurled 2d4+2 feet, suffer one point of damage per two feet thrown, and are deafened and stunned.
\par \tab The cone of force is considered to have a Strength of 19 for purposes o
f opening locked, barred, or magically held doors. This spell can move objects weighing up to 640 pounds a maximum distance of 4d4+4 feet. Fragile items must make a saving throw vs. crushing blow or be destroyed.
\par \tab The material components are a vial of rain gathered during a thunderstorm and the wizard's staff, which must be made of oak. The staff is not destroyed during casting. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Turn Pebble to Boulder}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) Reversible }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab At the culmination of this spell, the caster hurls a pebble which grows and increases in speed, becoming a deadly boulder that inflicts 3d6+8 points of damage if it strikes the target. (The rules for boulders as missile weap
ons apply as described in the }{\i\fs24 DUNGEON MASTER}{\fs24 
 Guide. ) The caster's THAC0 is used to determine success, and the caster is considered to be proficient with the thrown pebble and receives no penalty for range. The maximum range of attack is equal to 50 feet p
lus 10 feet per level of the caster. Only the caster may throw the pebble.
\par \tab The wizard can enchant one stone at 7th level and gains one stone per three levels of experience thereafter (two stones at 10th level, three at 13th level, etc.). Only one pebble m
ay be thrown per round, and pebbles must be hurled in consecutive rounds. The spell has a duration in rounds equal to the number of pebbles enchanted. Each pebble requires a separate attack roll. Pebbles may be thrown at different targets within range.

\par \tab The material components are pebbles, which revert to normal size when the spell expires.
\par \tab The reverse of this spell, }{\i\fs24 turn boulder to pebble}{\fs24 , shrinks a boulder to the size of a pebble. It affects only naturally occurring rocks and can not be used to shrink a statue or a cut gemstone.
\par \tab The number of rocks that may be affected is equal to the number of experience levels of the caster. Boulders must not exceed one cubic foot per level of the caster. Thus, a 10th-level wizard could shrink 10 rocks, each of which i
s equal to or less than 10 cubic feet in size. All rocks are affected in the same round the spell is cast. Though they need not be touched, the boulders must be within 50 feet of the caster. Boulders that have been shrunk remain so until dispelled. 

\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Unluck*}{\b\fs24  (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 10 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 2d10 rounds
\par Casting Time: 4
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab With this spell, the wild mage creates a negative pattern in the random forces surrounding one creature. The creatur
e is allowed a saving throw; if successful, the spell fails. If the saving throw is failed, random chance falls into an unlucky pattern. Any action involving random chance (i.e., any time a die roll affects the character) performed by the victim during th
e next 2-20 rounds requires two separate attempts; the worse result is always applied. (The victim rolls twice for attacks, damages, saving throws, etc., always using the worse die roll.)
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 luckstone}{\fs24  or similar magical device will negate }{\i\fs24 unluck}{\fs24 . Doing so, however, prevents the magical item from functioning for 2d10 rounds.
\par \tab The material component is a piece of a broken mirror. 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs36\cf2 Fifth-Level Spells }{\fs24 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Far Reaching III}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Component: V
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell operates exactly like the 3rd-level }{\i\fs24 far reaching I}{\fs24  spell except that the range of any spell of levels 1-3 is increased by 150% and the range of any 4th- or 5th-level spell is increased by 50%. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Khazid's Procurement }{\b\fs24 (Divination, Summoning) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Special
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 1 turn
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows the caster to more easily access rare or dangerous spell components. The wizard casts this spe
ll upon a silver mirror while concentrating on a mental image of the material he desires. The base chance of success is 50%, modified by the following factors: 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 +1% per level of the caster
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 +10% if the caster has seen the same type of substance or object before; this bonus is 
\par \tab not cumulative with the following bonus 
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 +20% if the caster has a sample of the material or the same type of object in his 
\par \tab possession; this bonus is not cumulative with the bonus above 
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 +30% if the wizard knows the location of the desired object 
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 -50% if the caster has never seen the same type of material or item before 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab If the percentile roll indicates failure, the caster is unable to locate the desired ingredient and the spell ends. If the roll indicates success, the wi
zard has located the object or substance and the mirror becomes a magical gate through which the caster can see the target. The size of the gate is determined by the size of the mirror, to a maximum size of 3 feet by 2 feet.
\par \tab The gate always appears within
 arm's length of the target, allowing the wizard to reach through the mirror, grasp the object of his desire, and draw it back through the gate. The wizard must risk his own safety--the gate does not allow the use of probes, long-handled ladles, tongs, or
 other equipment to gather the material. The caster cannot move completely through the gate.
\par \tab The gate vanishes when the spell's duration expires or when the target or the wizard moves more than 10' away from it.
\par \tab The gate is visible from both sides, and ot
her creatures can reach through the gate. Breath weapons, gaze attacks, missiles, spells, and similar attacks cannot be cast through the gate. Because creatures can pass their limbs through the gate, physical attacks and touch spells can be used.
\par \tab The only
 limit to the range of this spell is that the caster and the target must be on the same plane of existence. Elemental forces (not creatures) will not pass through the gate. Thus, the wizard does not run the risk of flooding his laboratory by opening a gat
e beneath the sea, for example. However, the spell does not provide any sort of protection against a hostile environment.
\par \tab The material components are an exquisite silver mirror of no less than 10,000 gp value and a black opal worth at least 1,000 gp which 
must be powdered and sprinkled on the mirror. The mirror is not lost after casting and may be used again, but the powdered opal is consumed in the casting. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Lower Resistance}{\b\fs24  (Abjuration, Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 60 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn+1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Using this spell, a wizard may attempt to reduce the magic resistance of a target creature. The magic resistance of the victim works against the }{\i\fs24 lower resistance}{\fs24  spell itself, bu
t at only half its normal value. No saving throw is permitted in addition to magic resistance.
\par \tab If the victim does not resist the effects of this spell, his magic resistance is reduced by a base 30% plus 1% per experience level of the wizard casting the spell.
\par \tab This spell has no effect on creatures that have no magic resistance.
\par \tab The material component is a broken iron rod.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Magic Staff}{\b\fs24  (Enchantment/Charm) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: Special
\par Area of Effect: The wizard's staff
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows a wizard's staff to store one spell level for every three levels of the caster. Thus, a 9th-level wizard can store three spell levels (three 1st-level spells, one 1st and one 2nd, or one 3rd-level spell).
\par \tab Spel
ls that are to be stored in the staff must be memorized normally by the wizard. The spells are then cast as normal when charging the staff; casting requires the spell's normal casting time plus one round. The spell is wiped from memory and material compon
ents are consumed. All spells to be stored must be cast into the staff within 1 turn.
\par \tab All stored spells have a casting time of 1.
\par \tab Spells remain in the staff until cast or dispelled, or up to 1 hour per level of the caster. After this time, all stored spells fade away.
\par \tab Only wizards who know the }{\i\fs24 magic staff}{\fs24 
 spell can cast spells from another wizard's staff. This applies to wizards who have never learned or could not normally cast the spells stored in a staff. It is common, however, for the staff's owner to 
implement a command word which must be known by anyone wishing to use the staff.
\par \tab The material component for this spell is a staff cut from an ash tree. For each spell level the wizard intends to imbue into the staff, it must be inlaid with rubies worth at least 1,000 gp. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Mind Fog }{\b\fs24 (Enchantment/Charm) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 80 yards
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 3 turns
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: 20-foot cube
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 mind fog}{\fs24  is a physical block of fog that enables the wizard to weaken the mental resistance of his victims. Victims are allowed a saving throw at a -2 penalty to avoid the effects.
\par \tab A creature who falls victim to the }{\i\fs24 mind fog}{\fs24  suffers -2 penalties to all saving throws against two categories of magic: all spells of the illusion/phantasm and enc
hantment/charm schools that affect the mind directly; and spells of 1st through 5th level which affect the mind directly. For example, }{\i\fs24 phantasmal force}{\fs24  is a mind-affecting spell; }{\i\fs24 phantom steed}{\fs24  is not.
\par \tab The penalty to saving throws operates cumulatively with any penalties that operate for other reasons. Affected creatures suffer the penalty as long as they remain in the fog and for 2d6 rounds thereafter. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Safeguarding}{\b\fs24  (Abjuration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn+1 turn/level
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: 15-foot-radius sphere
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab Use of this spell protects the wizard and anyone in the area of effect from damage caused by the rebounding of the wizard's spells. This includes damage from a }{\i\fs24 fireball}{\fs24  cast in an area too small for its effects, a reflected }{
\i\fs24 lightning bolt}{\fs24 , or any other offensive area spell that overlaps the }{\i\fs24 safeguarding's}{\fs24 
 area of effect. The protection is effective against spells of 7th level and lower. The protection does not apply to damage from spells rebounded by
 any form of magical spell turning. This spell does not protect the wizard against damage from spells or attacks cast by enemies or other party members.
\par \tab A wizard who has cast }{\i\fs24 safeguarding}{\fs24  is free to move and act normally. The spell's effect is always centered on him, regardless of his actions. Other creatures are free to enter and exit the area of effect.
\par \tab An area spell cast by the wizard will take effect normally, but its effects will be negated within the area of the }{\i\fs24 safeguarding}{\fs24  spell. This applies }{\i\fs24 only}{\fs24  to area spells centered outside the radius of the }{\i\fs24 
safeguarding}{\fs24  spell. If the wizard casts an offensive area spell within the area of the }{\i\fs24 safeguarding}{\fs24 , the }{\i\fs24 safeguarding}{\fs24  is immediately negated and those within the area suffer full damage from the spell. The
 wizard is free to cast non-offensive area spells and individually targeted spells within the area of the }{\i\fs24 safeguarding}{\fs24 .
\par \tab The material component is a piece of preserved skin from any creature that possesses natural magic resistance. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Von Gasik's Refusal}{\b\fs24  (Abjuration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 10 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 hour/level
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: 20-foot-square/level
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This powerful spell is designed to prevent unauthorized spellcasters from entering a hallway, doorway, window, or other point of entry.
\par \tab The spell creates an invisible barrier that blocks the targeted area. Any nonspellcasters and those spellcasters specifically named by the caster may pass freely. All other spellcasters collide with the invisible barrier. Me
mbers of classes with lesser spellcasting abilities (paladins, rangers, and bards) are blocked only if the character is of sufficient level to cast spells.
\par \tab The wizard is able to ward one area up to 20'-square for each level of his experience. Thus, a 12th
-level wizard may protect a square area 240 feet on a side. The area of effect may be divided among several smaller portals as long as the total area does not exceed the caster's limit. Each portal must be in range and sight of the caster at the time the 
spell is cast.
\par \tab The barriers exist for one hour per level of the caster unless they are dismissed by the caster or dispelled by a }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24  spell. A }{\i\fs24 disintegrate}{\fs24  spell immediately destroys a barrier, as does a }{\i\fs24 
rod of cancellation}{\fs24  or a }{\i\fs24 sphere of annihilation}{\fs24 .
\par \tab The invisible walls are not affected by physical blows, cold, heat, or electricity. Thrown and projected weapons (both magical and mundane) are not repelled by the barrier and may pass through the area normally. Spells can be cast through the barrier
. }{\i\fs24 Dimension door, teleport}{\fs24 , and similar effects can bypass the barriers.
\par \tab The material component is a pinch of dust from any wizard's tomb. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Vortex* }{\b\fs24 (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1d4 rounds+1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of effect: 5-foot-diameter circle
\par Saving Throw: \'bd
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  is a swirling mass of magical energy, barely controllable by the caster. On the round of casting, a small sparkle of lights fills the air at the desired position. On the second round, a 7'-tall, m
ulticolored tornado appears. From this moment on, the caster must maintain concentration in order for the }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  to remain.
\par \tab Each round, the caster can move the }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  60 feet. However, control of direction is not perfect. The caster has complete control over distance, but can only suggest the desired direction. The caster has a 50% chance of moving the }
{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  in the direction he desires; if the die roll indicates failure, the }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  moves according to the scatter diagram for grenade-like missiles. Thus, the }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24 
 usually moves in the general direction desired, but on occasion, it may move to either side or directly toward the caster.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  cannot pass through objects larger than its area of effect (it could move through a sapling but not an ancient o
ak tree) and will be redirected by these, rebounding along the general line of movement. For example, if cast in a narrow hallway, the }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  might ricochet down the hall, bouncing from side to side.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  is composed of raw magical energy. Nonmagical creatures struck by the }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24 
 suffer 1d4 points of damage per level of the caster. Magical creatures and spellcasters suffer 1d6 points of damage per level of the caster. Creatures struck are allowed a saving throw vs. magic to suffer only half damage.
\par \tab Each time a creature is struck, there is a 5% chance that the }{\i\fs24 vortex}{\fs24  will explode in a wild surge. Use Table 2 to determine the results of any wild surge. If the }{\i\fs24 vortex }{\fs24 
causes a wild surge, the spell ends immediately.
\par \tab The material components are a silk streamer and a handful of straw. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Waveform*}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 40 yards
\par Components: S, M
\par Duration: 1d10 rounds
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: 10-foot-cube/level
\par Saving Throw: \'bd
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab By means of this spell, the wild mage is able to shape and direct the patt
erns of water currents, allowing him to mold liquids into a variety of forms. The spell affects a quantity of liquid no larger than the area of effect. If cast onto a larger body, such as an ocean or large lake, the spell affects only the water within the
 area of effect.
\par \tab After casting }{\i\fs24 waveform}{\fs24 , the mage can form the water into any desired shape. The spell does not bind the liquid together in any fashion; it is still limited by its fluid properties and gravity. Thus, a mage could not use }{\i\fs24 
waveform}{\fs24  to create 
a humanoid creature with arms and legs and direct it to walk across land. He could, however, create a roughly human shape with flowing arms that rises out of the water, crashes forward in a huge splash, then rises and repeats the process. Other possible s
hapes include gigantic waves, geysers, whirlpools, and troughs.
\par \tab The shape takes one round to form, after which it can be maintained by concentration. The shape can be directed to move in any direction at the rate of 90 feet per round. If the }{\i\fs24 waveform}{\fs24  moves
 into or through a body of water, the form loses no intensity. However, if the wave is moved over dry ground, it loses one die of damage for every 10 feet crossed.
\par \tab If propelled against a target, the }{\i\fs24 waveform}{\fs24  causes 1d4 points of damage per level of the caster to creatures in its path. The }{\i\fs24 waveform}{\fs24 
 can be directed against creatures on the surface or underwater. Those struck are allowed a saving throw; success indicates half damage.
\par \tab If the victims are in or on a body of water, the shape will sweep them alon
g. Creatures of small size are carried with the form, moving at its speed. Medium and large size creatures are swept along at half the water's speed. Creatures larger than this resist the movement. Those caught in the current can make a Strength check eac
h round to swim free of the current.
\par \tab Boats and ships are particularly vulnerable to the }{\i\fs24 waveform}{\fs24 . If the }{\i\fs24 waveform}{\fs24 
 is twice the size of the vessel or more, the ship must make a seaworthiness check (as described in Table 77 of the DMG ). Vessels passing the 
check suffer damage as described above, reducing seaworthiness ratings for future checks by 2d6 points until repairs are made.
\par \tab Alternatively, this spell can be cast directly at a single water-based creature--a water weird, water elemental, or other creatu
re from the elemental plane of water. In this case, the spell causes 1d6 points of damage per level of the caster. The effect is instantaneous and the spell ends immediately after the attack is made.
\par \tab The material component is a small, carved oar decorated with aquamarines worth at least 500 gp. The oar disintegrates when the spell is cast. 
\par 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs36\cf2 Sixth-Level Spells }{\fs24 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Augmentation II}{\b\fs24  (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 3 turns
\par Casting Time: 6
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell functions exactly like the 3rd-level }{\i\fs24 augmentation I}{\fs24  spell except that five spells of levels 1-3 may be affected. For each die of damage caused by augmented spells, one hit point is added to the damage total.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Augmentation II}{\fs24  affects the first five spells which cause direct damage that are cast within the duration of the }{\i\fs24 augmentation II}{\fs24  spell. Only spells that cause direct physical damage are affected by this spell.

\par \tab The material component is a pair of concentric circles of gold or platinum. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24  }{\b\fs24\cf2 Bloodstone's Spectral Steed}{\b\fs24  (Necromancy) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 10 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 hour/level
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows a wizard to create a quasi-real, vulturelike creature. The flying steed can carr
y the caster and one other person per three levels of the wizard's experience (four at 12th level, five at 15th, etc.). All passengers must be specifically named during the casting.
\par \tab The spectral steed looks like a huge, skeletal vulture with tattered wing
s. As it flies, it utters hideous screeches that echo through the sky. The spectral steed flies at a movement rate of 4 per level of the caster, to a maximum movement rate of 48. It appears with a bit and bridle, plus one saddle per passenger.
\par \tab All normal animals shun the spectral steed and only monsters will attack it. The mount has AC 2 and 10 hit points plus 1 hit point per level of the caster. If it loses all of its hit points, the spectral steed disappears. It has no attack mode.

\par \tab The material component is a hollow bone from a vulture's wing, which must be carved into a whistle and blown when the spell is cast.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Claws of the Umber Hulk}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn/level
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When this spell is cast, the subject's hands widen and his fingernails thicken and grow, becoming equivalent in size and power to the iron-like claws of an umber hulk. The transformation takes one full round and is excruciatingly pai
nful, requiring a system shock roll. A failed roll causes the subject to suffer 3d4 points of damage.
\par \tab The subject can burrow as an umber hulk, cutting through 10 feet of solid stone or 60 feet of soil per turn. The only limitation to this is the subject's
 stamina; at the end of each turn of burrowing, the subject must succeed a Constitution check or be forced to rest for one turn.
\par \tab Burrowing through soil does not necessarily create a passable tunnel. If the subject wishes to make a passage in which others 
can travel or that he can exit when the spell ends, he must dig at a rate of 30 feet per turn. Cutting a tunnel through solid rock does not require extra care or time.
\par \tab The recipient of this spell can make two claw attacks per round, each inflicting 2d6 po
ints of damage plus any Strength bonuses. Each attack is made with a -2 penalty to hit. This penalty applies until the subject has made two successful consecutive attacks (not necessarily in the same round), at which time he is accustomed to using the cla
ws. The penalty is dropped for the remainder of the spell.
\par \tab The material component is an umber hulk's claw. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Dilation II}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Component: V
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell functions exactly like the 4th-level }{\i\fs24 dilation I }{\fs24 
spell, except that the area of effect of a 1st-, 2nd-, or 3rd- level spell is extended by 50%. Alternatively, the wizard may extend the area of effect of one 4th- or 5th-level spell by 25%.  
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Forest's Fiery Constrictor}{\b\fs24  (Conjuration/Summoning) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 10 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 6
\par Area of Effect: One source of fire
\par Saving Throw: Special
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell causes a tentacle of magical flame to snake forth from any existing source o
f natural or magical fire. The flaming tendril is 10 feet long, has AC 7, can be hit only by magical weapons of +2 or better, and has hit points equal to double the caster's level.
\par \tab Any creature within 20 feet of the tentacle is subject to attack as direct
ed by the caster. The victim must attempt a saving throw; if successful, the subject has avoided entanglement, but suffers 1d6 points of fire damage from contact with the tendril. If the saving throw is failed, the victim is entangled by the flaming serpe
nt and suffers 3d6 points of fire damage each round until the tendril is destroyed or the spell expires.
\par \tab If the fire source from which the tentacle emanates is extinguished, the remaining time that the fiery constrictor may exist is cut in half.
\par \tab The material component is a red dragon's scale. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Lorloveim's Shadowy Transformation }{\b\fs24 (Illusion)}{\b\fs24\cf2  }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 1d4 rounds+1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 6
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When this spell is cast, the illusionist t
ransforms one creature or a specified amount of non-living material into shadow, making it insubstantial. Thus, a door could be turned to shadow and entered. The maximum amount of inanimate material that may be transformed is one cubic foot per level of t
he caster.
\par \tab Unwilling creatures are allowed a saving throw to resist the }{\i\fs24 shadowy transformation}{\fs24 . Magical items and the magical effects of spells (such as }{\i\fs24 Bigby's forceful hand}{\fs24  or a }{\i\fs24 wall of stone}{\fs24 
 ) cannot be affected.
\par \tab A transformed creature and all its gear become insubstantial. The creature can pass through small holes, narrow openings, and the smallest cracks. The creature cannot fly without additional magic.
\par \tab No form of attack is possible when in shadow form except against creatures that exist on the Ethe
real plane. In this case, all attacks are normal; however, the shadowy creature may be harmed only by magical weapons of +1 or greater or by creatures able to affect those struck only by magical weapons. Spells and special attacks have normal effects.

\par \tab Most undead creatures will ignore a creature in shadow form, believing it to be a wraith or spectre; however, liches and powerful undead may save vs. spell with a -4 penalty to recognize the spell. A successful }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24 
 spell forces the creature in shadow form back to normal form. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Wildshield*}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell cloaks the caster in a whirling band of scintillating colors, completely concealing him. The caster is able to see normally within and outside the shield.
\par \tab The }{\i\fs24 wildshield}{\fs24  protects the caster from the effects of spells and magical items. The shield can completely absorb 2d6 spell levels (i.e., if the roll of 2d6 results in 10, t
he shield could absorb ten 1st-level spells, two 5th-level spells, or any similar combination), thereby negating their effects on the caster. Both area effect spells and those individually targeted at the wild mage can be absorbed. In the case of area spe
lls, the }{\i\fs24 wildshield}{\fs24  protects only the mage. All others in the area of effect suffer normal effects from the spell.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Wildshield}{\fs24  also protects against wild surges, whether caused by the caster's magic or by an outside source. Each wild surge is considered equal to 1d6 spell levels.
\par \tab The spell remains in effect until it is either canceled by the caster or it reaches its spell level capacity. If the capacity is met exactly, the }{\i\fs24 wildshield}{\fs24  simply ceases to function. However, if the }{\i\fs24 wildshield}{\fs24 
 is struck by more sp
ell levels than it can absorb, it explodes in a wild surge. The spell that triggered the surge is completely negated, its energy instead transformed into a wild surge (see Table 2). Since the shield no longer functions, the formerly protected wizard is su
bject to full effects of this wild surge.
\par \tab The material component is a small sponge. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Wildstrike*}{\b\fs24  (Conjuration/Summoning) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 2d4 rounds
\par Casting Time: 6
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell is used primarily against hostile spellcasters. It distorts all attempts at spellcasting, converting spell energy into wild surges.
\par \tab The victim of a }{\i\fs24 wildstrike}{\fs24  is allowed a saving throw; if successful, the spell has no effect. If the saving throw is faile
d, the target is enclosed within a field of wild magic. If the victim casts spells or uses a charge from a magical item, a wild surge is automatically created (refer to Table 2). When determining the effects of this surge, the true level of the wild mage 
who cast the }{\i\fs24 wildstrike}{\fs24  is subtracted from the die roll, making the effects of the wild surge more likely to affect the victim.
\par \tab The material component is a small glass tube that is shattered in the casting. 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs36\cf2 
\par Seventh-Level Spells }{\fs24 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Acid Storm}{\b\fs24  (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 10 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 7
\par Area of Effect: 40-foot-diameter circle
\par Saving Throw: \'bd 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This deadly spell unleashes a downpour of magical, gelatinous acid droplets. All creatures within the area of effect are coated by globs of gooey acid. The acid can be washed off only with wine, vinegar, or by a successful }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{
\fs24  or similar spell. The acid remains present for 1 round per level of the caster, then vanishes.
\par \tab Creatures coated by the acid suffer 1d
4 hit points of damage each round during rounds 1-3, 1d6 points in each of rounds 4-6, and 1d8 points on each round thereafter. Characters who successfully save vs. spells during the first round suffer only half damage from the acid for the remaining roun
ds. When the spell expires, no further damage is inflicted.
\par \tab Acid damage can be healed through any means except regeneration. The material component is a drop of acid. 
\par  
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Bloodstone's Frightful Joining}{\b\fs24  (Necromancy) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 1 turn/level
\par Casting Time: 7
\par Area of Effect: One undead creature
\par Saving Throw: Special 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When this powerful spell is employed, the wizard transfers his spirit to the body of an undead creature, totally dominating it. If the undead creature has intelligence
, it is allowed a saving throw vs. spell to resist the joining. If the save is successful, the caster's spirit is forced back into his own body. The wizard must make a system shock roll; if the roll fails, the wizard suffers 5d6 points of damage. If the r
oll succeeds, the wizard suffers half this damage.
\par \tab If the creature's save fails, the necromancer joins his life essence with that of the undead. While in the creature's body, the caster can use all of its special attacks and innate abilities, excluding spells memorized by the creature.
\par \tab The wizard's body remains comatose, is subject to all regular attacks, and suffers damage normally. The wizard's spirit can travel an unlimited distance from his physical body as long as they remain on the same plane of existence.
\par \tab If intelligent, the possessed undead continually tries to purge the caster with mental threats that can be heard only by the wizard. The thoughts of the undead are ghastly. During the first minute of each hour of possession, the caster must succeed
 an Intelligence check in order to retain his sanity. The roll is modified by the difference between the creature's Intelligence and that of the spellcaster. If the undead has a higher score, the difference is added to the die roll. If the necromancer has
 a higher Intelligence, the difference is subtracted from the roll.
\par \tab If the roll is successful, nothing happens and the caster may continue to possess the undead. If the Intelligence roll fails, the wizard's intellect degenerates, making him a raving, homic
idal maniac. His spirit is immediately forced to return to his body, and he must attempt a system shock roll with damage occurring as outlined above. The caster remains dangerously insane until a }{\i\fs24 heal}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 wish}{\fs24 
 spell is used to restore his intellect.
\par \tab This spell can be very useful when combined with the }{\i\fs24 mask of death}{\fs24  spell.
\par \tab When the spell's duration expires, the necromancer's spirit immediately returns to his body. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Hatch the Stone from the Egg }{\b\fs24 (Alteration, Enchantment, Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 1d4+4 hours
\par Area of Effect: One alchemical mixture
\par Saving Throw: None 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When a wizard wishes to create the magical item known as the }{\i\fs24 philosopher's stone}{\fs24 , he must first discover its alchemical formula, which tells hi
m the necessary ingredients and the method of preparing them. This information is not provided by this spell, and this spell is useless without the formula. (The exact ingredients and formula are decided by the Dungeon Master and must be discovered by the
 wizard by adventuring.)
\par \tab When the formula has been discovered and the ingredients prepared, the wizard enchants the alchemical mixture with the }{\i\fs24 enchant an item}{\fs24  spell. }{\i\fs24 Hatch the stone from the egg}{\fs24 
 is then cast upon the mixture. This spell slowly transmutes the mixture into its final form as the philosopher's stone. The process is completed with a }{\i\fs24 permanency}{\fs24  spell.
\par \tab The material component for this spell is a magical item known as the }{\i\fs24 philosopher's egg}{\fs24 , which is an enchanted retort used to hold the alchemical 
mixture. The egg is not destroyed upon completion of the spell and may be used again. (Further details about the }{\i\fs24 philosopher's egg}{\fs24  are found in Chapter 4 of this book.) 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Hornung's Surge Selector*}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab The great Hornung, having been blasted more than once by his own wild surges, devised a method of improving the results of wild magic and, not incidentally, his own chances of survival. The result was }{\i\fs24 Hornung's surge selector}{\fs24 .

\par \tab By casting this spell, the wild mage gains greater control over wild surges. When the caster's spell creates a wild surge, two separate results are determined from Table 2. The caster can then choose which of th
e two results will take effect. This spell can be used in conjunction with}{\i\fs24  Nahal's reckless dweomer.}{\fs24 
\par \tab The spell's duration is a fixed number of surges or 12 hours, whichever comes first. The wild mage is able to shape one wild surge per five levels of his 
experience; thus, a 15th-level caster could shape three wild surges within a 12-hour period. At the end of 12 hours, the spell expires, regardless of the number of surges remaining.
\par \tab The material component is a brass spinner. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Intensify Summoning}{\b\fs24  (Conjuration/Summoning, Necromancy)}{\fs24 
\par Range: Special
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn
\par Casting Time: 6
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell enhances the strength of creatures summoned by the caster via 1st through 6th level conjuration/summoning spells. Only spells which bring summoned creatures to the wizard are affected.
\par \tab The first two conjuration/summoning spells cast by the wizard within one turn following the intensify summoning spell are affected. Summoned creatures gain 2 hit points per 
hit die. The affected creatures retain their bonus hit points until the normal expiration of the spell that summoned them. 
\par \tab The material components are a small leather pouch and a miniature silver candelabra. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Malec-Keth's Flame Fist}{\b\fs24  (Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 1
\par Area of Effect: One creature or object
\par Saving Throw: Special 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When this spell is completed, one of the caster's hands (his choice) bursts into light and is surrounded by an aura of flame. The caster suffers no damage from this effect. Illumination is equal to that of a torch.
\par \tab If the wizard successfully touches an opponent, the subject must attempt a saving throw. If the roll is successful, the flame remains on the caster's hand (and he may use it
 to make further attacks until the spell's duration expires) and the touched creature suffers 1d4+2 points of fire damage. If the save is failed, the flame leaves the caster's hand to surround the victim's body in an aura of searing fire. The superheated 
aura burns for 1 round, inflicting 1d4 points of damage per level of the caster.
\par \tab Instead of attacking a creature, the caster may choose to touch any single object, which is automatically surrounded by the searing aura for 1 round and must succeed at an ite
m saving throw vs. magical fire or be destroyed. The aura can surround an object up to 5 cubic feet in volume per level of the caster. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Shadowcat }{\b\fs24 (Illusion) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 10 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 turn/level
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When this spell is cast, the wizard brings into being a cat made of shadow. The }{\i\fs24 shadowcat}{\fs24  is the size of a normal cat and may be either grey or black at the caster's option. The caster has complete telepathic control of the fe
line; he can see, hear, and even speak through it as long as it remains within range. At the moment it moves out of range, the }{\i\fs24 shadowcat}{\fs24  vanishes. The caster does not need to concentrate on the }{\i\fs24 shadowca}{\fs24 t.
\par \tab The shadowy feline is insubstantial, making subjec
t only to magical or special attacks, including those by weapons of +1 or better. It has AC 5, a movement rate of 18, and saving throws equal to those of the caster. The cat dissipates if it loses hit points equal to one-half the caster's total hit points
. The }{\i\fs24 shadowcat}{\fs24  has no attacks of its own and cannot touch or carry objects. A successful }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24  spell causes the cat to vanish.
\par \tab A }{\i\fs24 shadowcat}{\fs24  makes no sound as it moves. It is 90% undetectable in all but the brightest conditions. It can pass through small holes or narrow openings.
\par \tab The material components of this spell are a black pearl of at least 100 gp value and a claw from a grey or black cat. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Spell Shape*}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1d4+1 rounds
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: Special 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell gives the wild mage the ability to seize magical energy directed at him and reshape it as he desires. While it is in effect, the spell gives no visible sign of its existence. It offers no protection against area effect spells.
\par \tab If a wild mage is the target of a spell or magical item, this spell automatically allows him a saving throw. If the saving throw is failed, the opponent's spell has normal effects. If the saving throw is successful, the }{\i\fs24 spell shape}{\fs24 
 absorbs the magical energy of the opponent's spell. The wild mage can then choose to let the energy dissipate or he can instantly use it to cast a spell back at the opposing mage. The return spell must be of an equal or lesser spell level than the 
original one and must be currently memorized by the mage. The act of returning the spell does not cost the wild mage any of his memorized spells. Spell energy cannot be saved; if not used immediately, it dissipates.
\par \tab For example, Hamos, a wild mage, is protected by a }{\i\fs24 spell shape}{\fs24  and is struck by a }{\i\fs24 finger of death}{\fs24 
 (a 7th-level spell). He succeeds at his saving throw and is now able to cast a spell of 7th level or lower. Hamos currently has }{\i\fs24 feeblemind}{\fs24  memorized. Since it is only a 5th-level spell, he chooses 
to cast it back at his enemy. He makes his level variation check (and doesn't get a wild surge) and the }{\i\fs24 feeblemind}{\fs24  is sent hurtling back at his foe. Hamos still has his original }{\i\fs24 feeblemind}{\fs24 
 memorized. The remaining two spell levels are lost, since they were not used in the same round.
\par \tab If a wild mage is struck by two spells at once, he may choose which spell to shape. He suffers all effects of the remaining spell.
\par \tab The material component is a diamond worth no less than 2,000 gp. When the spell is cast, the diamond is transformed into a lump of coal. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Steal Enchantment}{\b\fs24  (Enchantment) }{\fs24 
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Permanent
\par Casting Time: 1 hour
\par Area of Effect: One item
\par Saving Throw: Neg. 
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell "steals" the enchantment from a magical item a
nd places it within another, non-magical item (the material component). Both objects must be touched by the wizard during casting. The two items must be of the same category (blunt weapon, edged weapon, ring, amulet, shield, armor, wand, etc.).
\par \tab The enchan
tment can be transferred only to a nonmagical item. Only the energy of one item can be transferred; it is not possible to combine two magical items into one item. The new item has all the properties of the original magical item (including the same number 
of charges, if any).
\par \tab At the culmination of the spell, the original magical object is allowed an item saving throw vs. disintegration with all modifiers it is allowed as a magical item. Exceptionally powerful objects (such as artifacts) may be considered to
 automatically succeed the saving throw at the DM's discretion.
\par \tab If the saving throw is successful, the magical object resists the effect and the spell ends in failure. If the roll is failed, the magical item loses all of its powers, which are transferred to the previously nonmagical object.
\par \tab Even if the magical item fails its saving throw, the spell's success is not guaranteed. There is a chance that the enchantment might be lost. The base chance of this occurring is 100%, modified by -5% per level of the 
caster. Thus, a 20th-level wizard has no chance of losing the magic. If the enchantment is lost, both items become nonmagical.
\par \tab The material component is the nonmagical item which is to receive the enchantment. It must be of equal or greater value than the object to be drained.
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Suffocate}{\b\fs24  (Alteration, Necromancy) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 7
\par Area of Effect: 10-foot-radius circle
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell draws the breath out of all creatures within the area of effect who fail a saving throw. Their breath is placed within a small silk bag held by the caster.
\par \tab Each round, a victim of this spell must attempt a Constitution check. If failed, the creature suffers 2d4 points of damage. If successful, the subject has taken in enough air to reduce the damage to 1d4.
\par \tab As they struggle and gasp for air, affected creatures move and attack at half their normal rates, have a -4 Armor Class penalty, an attack penalty of -4, and lose all Dexterity combat bonuses.
\par \tab Effects of this spell continue each round regardless of whether the victims remain in the original area of effect. The damage accumulates until the spell expires, the silk bag is opened, or a successful }{\i\fs24 dispel magic}{\fs24 
 spell is cast upon the bag. The penalties to combat remain in effect for 1d3 rounds after the spell ends.
\par \tab The material component is a small silk bag studded with black opals worth a total of no less than 5,000 gp. The bag is not destroyed during casting, but becomes useless for future castings if a successful dispel magic spell is used on it. 
\par 
\par 
\par }{\b\fs36\cf2 Eighth-Level Spells }{\fs24 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting}{\b\fs24  (Alteration, Necromancy) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 20 yards/level
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: Instantaneous
\par Casting Time: 8
\par Area of Effect: 30-foot cube
\par Saving Throw: \'bd
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell evaporates moisture from the bodies of every living creature within the area of effect, inflicting 1d8 points of damage per level of the caster. Affected creatures are allowed a saving throw, with success indicating half damage.
\par \tab This spell is especially devastating to water elementals and plant creatures, who receive a penalty of -2 to their saving throws.
\par \tab The material component is a bit of sponge.
\par  
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Airboat}{\b\fs24  (Alteration, Enchantment) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 1 mile
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 1 hour/level
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell must be cast under a cloudy sky. The caster points at a cloud, which immediately descends toward him. As it comes closer, the cloud changes shape, becoming any sort of vessel imagined by t
he wizard (a dragon-shaped galley, a one-man dinghy, etc.).
\par \tab Although the airboat is made of cloud, it feels solid and can support the weight of the caster plus one passenger per level of the wizard. It can fly at any speed up to 5 miles per hour per level of the caster (to a maximum of 90 miles per hour).

\par \tab The caster maintains total telepathic control over the airboat's speed and direction. While controlling the vessel, the wizard is able to perform other actions but may not cast other spells. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Gunther's Kaleidoscopic Strike}{\b\fs24  (Invocation/Evocation) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 5 yards/level
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: Instantaneous
\par Casting Time: 8
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab When this spell is cast, a thin beam of shimmering, kaleidoscopic light shoots from the wizard's fingertips toward his target. The victim is allowed a saving throw to resist the beam.
\par \tab This spell has no effect on nonspellcasters, causing them no harm whatsoever. Creatures with innate spell-like abilities are also unaffected. Against wiza
rds and priests, this spell can be devastating. It "short-circuits" the arcane energy stored in a spellcaster's mind, wiping away a number of memorized spells. Lost spells must be rememorized. 
\par \tab The number of spells drained is equal to the caster's level m
inus 1d20. Thus, a 16th-level wizard drains a maximum of 15 spells, but could drain no spells depending on the die roll. After subtracting the die roll from the caster's level, any result of zero or a negative number indicates that the victim loses no spe
lls.
\par \tab Spells are drained from the wizard's memorized spells beginning with 1st-level spells and working up to higher level spells. Any decision regarding which spell should be drained from a specific level should be determined randomly. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Homunculus Shield}{\b\fs24  (Evocation, Necromancy) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: The caster
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab By creating a }{\i\fs24 homunculus shield}{\fs24 , the wizard separates a portion of his mind in the form of an exteriorized magical
 homunculus. This creature is invisible to all but the caster and appears as a miniature version of the caster perched atop the wizard's head.
\par \tab The wizard may move and act normally while this spell is in effect. The magical homunculus operates as an independent spellcaster. It may cast only }{\i\fs24 teleport, contingency}{\fs24 
, and protective spells of 4th level and lower. It casts only spells from the wizard's memorized store of spells, but any spells cast by the homunculus are done so with a casting time of 1. The wizar
d selects which spells are cast by his homunculus; after they are cast, they are wiped from the caster's memory.
\par \tab The homunculus has 1 hit point per two levels of the caster. These points are "borrowed" from the caster; while the homunculus is present, the wizard's hit points are reduced by this amount.
\par \tab The homunculus cannot be struck by melee or missile weapons separately from the wizard. It can be damaged separately from the wizard (e.g., by a }{\i\fs24 magic missile}{\fs24  targeted at the homunculus or by area effect sp
ells). The homunculus has the attributes and saving throws of the wizard.
\par \tab At the end of the spell's duration, the homunculus disappears and any hit points it had are restored to the wizard. Hit points lost by the homunculus can be regained only by magical healing. 
\par \tab If the wizard's hit points are reduced to zero at any time during the spell, the wizard is dead even if the homunculus had hit points remaining.
\par \tab A wizard with an active }{\i\fs24 homunculus shield}{\fs24  suffers a -4 saving throw penalty against magic jar spells cast upon him due to the division of his mental energy.
\par \tab The material component is a miniature sculpted bust of the spellcaster. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Hornung's Random Dispatcher* }{\b\fs24 (Abjuration) }{\fs24 
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Component: V
\par Duration: Instantaneous
\par Casting Time: 2
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab With the utterance of a few words, this spell can hurl a creature to a random plane and leave him there. The target, if unwilling, is allowed a saving throw. If successful, the spell fails. If unsuccessful, the victi
m and all items carried by him are sent to a random plane. To determine the plane, roll on the table below. 
