\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab A surface affected by }{\i\fs24 squeaking floors}{\fs24  squeaks loudly when any creature larger than a normal rat (larger than one-half cubic foot or weighing mor
e than three pounds) steps on it or touches it. The spell affects a square whose sides equal the caster's level times 10 feet (a 9th-level priest could affect a square whose sides are 90 feet long).
\par \tab The squeaks can be heard in a 100-foot radius, regardles
s of interposing barriers such as walls and doors. The squeaks occur regardless of the surface, whether wood, stone, dirt, or any other solid material. Listeners automatically know the direction of the sounds.
\par \tab Characters who successfully move silently reduce the radius of the noise to 50 feet. Those able to }{\i\fs24 fly}{\fs24  or otherwise avoid direct contact with the affected surface will not activate the }{\i\fs24 squeaking floor}{\fs24 .
\par \tab The material component is a rusty iron hinge that squeaks when moved. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Strength of One}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Sphere: Law
\par Range: 10 yards
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 2d6 rounds
\par Casting Time: 3
\par Area of Effect: One creature+1creature/2 levels
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab By casting this spell on a group of lawful creatures, the priest imbues each creature with a Strength
 bonus equal to that of the strongest creature in the group. To be affected by the spell, all creatures must touch the hand of the priest at the time of casting. Only human, demihuman, and humanoid creatures of man-size or smaller may be affected. The cha
racters can be a mixed group of Lawful Neutral, Lawful Good, or Lawful Evil alignments. The spell will not take effect if any creature of Neutral or Chaotic alignment is included in the group.
\par \tab Prior to casting, one creature is designated the keystone. There may never be more than one keystone in a group, even if another creature has equal strength.
\par \tab Upon completion of the spell, all affected characters gain a bonus to damage equal to the keystone's bonus to damage from Strength. Any magical bonuses belongin
g to the keystone are not added; only the keystone's natural strength is conferred on the group.
\par \tab This bonus supersedes any bonus a character might normally receive. Thus, a warrior with 16 Strength (a +1 bonus to damage) who benefits from this spell with 
a keystone who has Strength 18/07 (a damage bonus of +3) gains a total bonus of +3 to damage (not +4 to damage). The keystone receives no bonus.
\par \tab Affected creatures gain no improvements to THAC0, bend bars/lift gates, or other functions of Strength.
\par \tab The spell ends if the keystone is killed before the duration expires. The bonus and duration are not affected if a member of the group is killed within the duration of the spell. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Telepathy}{\b\fs24  (Divination, Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Sphere: Thought
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: 1 turn+2 rounds/level
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell establishes direct, two-way mental contact between the priest and a single subject. The subject must have Intelligence of at least 5 for the s
pell to take effect. While the spell is in effect, the two participants can communicate silently and rapidly, regardless of whether they share a common language.
\par  \tab }{\i\fs24 Telepathy}{\fs24  does not give either participant access to the other's thoughts, memories, or emotions. Participants can only "hear" the thoughts that the other participant actively "sends."
\par \tab Mind-to-mind communication is approximately four times faster than verbal communication. The level of complexity that can be communicated is only that which can b
e expressed through language. Gestures, expressions, and body language cannot be conveyed.
\par \tab A priest can establish separate "telepathic channels" to multiple individuals. Each linkage is established through a separate casting of the spell. There is no network between the channels. For example, Balfas the priest establishes }{\i\fs24 
