. Spells that normally affect more than one individual (such as confusion ) will affect only the selected subject when cast following }{\i\fs24 telethaumaturgy}{\fs24 .
\par \tab When }{\i\fs24 telethaumaturgy}{\fs24  is cast by a priest of 11th level or higher, it has an additional effect. If the target is within the normal range of the subsequent spell (e.g., 80 yards for }{\i\fs24 charm person}{\fs24 
), the subject's saving throw suffers a penalty of -2.
\par \tab Like the }{\i\fs24 personal reading}{\fs24  spell,}{\i\fs24   telethaumaturgy}{\fs24  functions only if the priest knows the correct name of his subject. If the priest casts the spell using an alias, he will not know that }{\i\fs24 telethaumaturgy}{
