\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Repeat Action}{\b\fs24  (Enchantment/Charm) }{\fs24 
\par Sphere: Time
\par Range: 30 yards
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: Special
\par Casting Time: 5
\par Area of Effect: One creature
\par Saving Throw: Neg.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par  \tab This spell compels its victim to repeat the action of the previous round. The result of the repetition is always identical to the original result. 
\par \tab For example, if a character fired an arrow and inflicted 4 points of damage, a }{\i\fs24 repeat action}{\fs24 
 spell will cause him to fire a second arrow that will also inflict 4 points of damage. As long as the victim of the first arrow is within range, the subject affected by }{\i\fs24 repeat action}{\fs24  will adjust his aim and fire the second a
rrow at him. If the victim of the arrow moves out of range, the subject will fire his second arrow in the direction of the recipient. If the recipient is out of sight, the subject will fire in the direction of the recipient's original location.
\par \tab The subject of a }{\i\fs24 repeat action}{\fs24 
 spell must be capable of performing the indicated action a second time. If a character has no arrows in his quiver, he cannot fire an arrow. If a wizard were ordered to repeat a spell, he would attempt the spell only if he had the spel
l memorized and had sufficient material components. If a subject discovered a gem during a given round, }{\i\fs24 repeat action}{\fs24  will only compel him to hunt again; he will not recover another gem unless a second gem is actually present. 
\par \tab An unwilling subject is allowed a saving throw vs. spell to resist the effects of }{\i\fs24 repeat action}{\fs24 .
\par \tab The material components are two identical glass spheres, each an inch or less in diameter. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Shrieking Walls}{\b\fs24  (Enchantment) }{\fs24 
\par Sphere: Wards
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 day/level
\par Casting Time: 1 turn
\par Area of Effect: 20'-cube
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell enchants any single room no larger than the area of effect. When any creature larger than a normal rat (larger than one-half cubic foot or weighing more than three pounds
) enters the room, shrill shrieks begin to emanate from the walls. The shrieks persist for 2-5 (1d4+1) rounds. The walls do not undergo any physical change.
\par \tab The shrieks can be heard only by creatures inside the room. Creatures hearing the shrieks experience no ill effects on the first round, allowing them time to leave the room or cover their ears. }{\i\fs24 Silence, 15' radius}{\fs24 
 protects against the effects.
\par \tab Creatures who remain in the room during the second or subsequent rounds of the shrieks who have not protected their hearing are penalized as follows:
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 Creatures whose levels or Hit Dice are greater than the level of the caster are stunned for 2-8 (2d4) rounds.
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 Creatures whose levels or Hit Dice are less than or equal to the level of the caster become deaf for 
1-4 hours, suffering a -1 penalty to surprise; deafened spellcasters have a 20% chance of miscasting any spell with a verbal component.
\par \tab The material components are a small golden bell and a bee's wing.  
