\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Thoughtwave}{\b\fs24  (Divination) }{\fs24 
\par Sphere: Divination
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S
\par Duration: Instantaneous
\par Casting Time: 1
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: Special
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This cooperative spell can be cast by either a single priest or a group of priests. }{\i\fs24 Thoughtwave}{\fs24  allows the priest to send a short but powerful mess
age to one or more specific individuals, informing them of his situation and general location. The spell instantly generates a powerful mental impulse indicative of the caster's general mental state--anger, fear, pain, despair, etc.
\par \tab The caster can designa
te as many as ten persons to receive this message, provided they can all be specifically named or grouped in a general category. Thus, the caster could designate a group of characters by name or could target "fellow priests," "superiors," "adventuring com
panions," "knights of Lord Harcourt," or "villagers of Dopp." If more than ten individuals are in the group, those closest to the source will receive the impulse.
\par \tab There is no range limitation to the spell, although it cannot be projected outside the plane occupied by the caster.
\par \tab Creatures receiving the impulse automatically know who sent it (even if they have never met the priest before) and gain a clear indication of the mood and situation of the caster. Recipients also intuitively know the general source
 of the spell, although they are unable to pinpoint rooms, dungeon levels, or landmarks. For example, a fighter could suddenly be struck by an image of Father Rastibon, who is injured and in great pain somewhere along the forest road. A priest might sudde
nly sense that his patriarch is being tortured in the dungeons of Castle Varrack.
\par \tab The spell can also be cast by more than one priest, allowing them to either contact greater numbers of individuals or increase the intensity of the message. If greater number
s are desired, ten characters are contacted per priest involved in the casting.
\par \tab Increasing the intensity of the message makes it more compelling. Doubling the intensity (requiring at least three priests) causes the message to act as a }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{\fs24 . In this 
case, the effect is limited to a single target. Tripling the intensity (requiring at least five priests) gives the spell the force of a }{\i\fs24 quest}{\fs24 
. This effect is also limited to a single target. In both cases, the target is allowed a saving throw to avoid the effect of the }{\i\fs24 suggestion}{\fs24  or }{\i\fs24 quest}{\fs24 . 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Time Pool}{\b\fs24  (Divination) }{\fs24 
\par Sphere: Time
\par Range: Touch
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 round/level
\par Casting Time: 1 round
\par Area of Effect: Special
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell allows the caster to cause a mirror, a pool of 
water, or any other reflective surface to reveal a specific event from the past. The image provides a perfectly clear picture with normal sounds, as if the caster were present at the scene. The image continues for the duration of the spell.
\par \tab }{\i\fs24 Time pool}{\fs24  will not reveal images from other planes of existence.
\par \tab The spell's success is not automatic. The caster must know the general nature of the event he wishes to view (i.e., "Show me the murder of King Thamak"). The caster's base chance of viewing the desired sc
ene is 50%, modified as follows, to a maximum of 90%:
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 Add 5% for each point of the caster's Wisdom above 15.
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 Add 20% if the caster has successfully used }{\i\fs24 time pool}{\fs24  to observe the same event 
\par \tab before. 
\par \tab Only one of the following may apply:
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 Add 20% if the event is one in which the caster participated.
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 Add 10% if the caster is well informed about the event.
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 Add 5% if the caster is slightly informed about the event.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 \tab The caster cannot communicate or otherwise interact with the image. Spells cannot be cast into the }{\i\fs24 time pool}{\fs24 .
\par \tab The material components are a suitable reflective surface and a pinch of powdered quartz. 
\par 
\par }\pard \keep\nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\b\fs24\cf2 Unceasing Vigilance of the Holy Sentinel}{\b\fs24  (Alteration) }{\fs24 
\par Sphere: Guardian
\par Range: 0
\par Components: V, S, M
\par Duration: 1 hour/level
\par Casting Time: 1 turn
\par Area of Effect: 5-foot-radius sphere
\par Saving Throw: None
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {\fs24 
\par \tab This spell enhances a priest's ability to guard a person, place, or object. The spell's effect must be centered on a specific area, for it creates an invisible spherical boundary up to 10 feet
 in diameter. The effect is not mobile; it cannot move with a living creature.
\par \tab While within the area of effect of this spell, the priest (and only the priest) gains several special abilities:
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 His sense of sight is magically enhanced. He can see through 
normal darkness and can see invisible creatures and objects. He cannot see through solid objects, however, and the range of his magical sight is limited to 60 feet.
\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 The priest has no need for food, water, or rest. He does not feel fatigue and regenerates 1 hit point per hour spent within the circle. However, he does not actually rest and therefore cannot regain spells until he sleeps.

\par \tab }{\fs24\cf2 \bullet }{\fs24 He is totally immune to the effects of magical and natural fear, as well as }{\i\fs24 sleep}{\fs24  and }{\i\fs24 charm}{\fs24  spells.
\par \tab If the priest leave
s the circle, the spell is broken. When the spell ends, the priest must rest for 1 turn per hour (or portion thereof) spent in the circle. If the priest is forced into action (by being attacked, for example), he can move at only half his normal movement r
ate, has an Armor Class penalty of -2, an attack penalty of -2, and loses all Dexterity combat bonuses.
\par \tab To cast this spell, the priest must trace a circle of sigils and runes 10 feet in diameter using a special ink containing the powder of a crushed sapphire (at least 1,000 gp value) and a drop of holy water. This procedure takes 1 turn to complete. 

